=== RULES ===
- READ BOTH SECTIONS: Use PLAYER'S INTENT for *what the player wanted to do*, and
  WHAT HAPPENED for *what mechanically occurred*. If the intent describes a sustained
  effort but the outcome describes only the mechanical result, estimate time for the
  sustained effort.
- COMPOUND ACTIONS: If the intent chains actions ("rest then travel", "craft and then
  head out"), estimate the FIRST time-consuming action only. The rest comes back next turn.
- SUSTAINED ACTIONS: When the intent uses "until", "keep doing", "wait for", "continue
  until", "watch for", "stand guard", or otherwise indicates persistent activity until a
  result or event, estimate the TOTAL expected duration — not a single brief attempt. The
  mechanical outcome may say "nothing happened" but the TIME still passes. Examples:
    "wait until something happens"       → 1–4 hours (standing guard)
    "hunt until I catch something"       → 1–4 hours (Survival activity)
    "search until I find it"             → 0.5–2 hours (extended search)
    "sit and observe, waiting"           → 1–4 hours (guard duty)
  Lean toward the higher end when in doubt. An uneventful wait is still a wait.
- TAKE 20: If the outcome mentions "Take 20" or "auto-resolved via Take 20", the
  character spent ~40 minutes (0.67 hours) carefully repeating the check.
- OBSERVATION DURATION: Distinguish incidental glances from sustained observation.
  INSTANT (0.0017 hours, only out-of-combat-flavour glance): "I look at the table",
    "I glance at the sign", "what do I see?", "I look around" — single-moment perception.
  SUSTAINED (0.17–0.5 hours): "I carefully survey the area", "I watch the entrance",
    "I pay close attention to the crowd", "I scan for threats" — deliberate, extended focus.

Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences). `hours_elapsed` is required.
